WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:02.270
- Please welcome to the
show, our dear friend,

00:00:02.270 --> 00:00:03.880
Danny Pellegrino.

00:00:03.880 --> 00:00:05.931
(crowd cheers)
(applause)

00:00:05.931 --> 00:00:07.069
- [Danny] Excited to be here.

00:00:07.069 --> 00:00:08.179
- [Drew] Thanks.

00:00:08.179 --> 00:00:11.190
And you've been published a lot of times,

00:00:11.190 --> 00:00:14.330
but this is all you.

00:00:14.330 --> 00:00:16.440
- Yeah, I was a ghost writer
before, so this is my first

00:00:16.440 --> 00:00:19.030
collection of stories, so it
was so creatively fulfilling

00:00:19.030 --> 00:00:21.330
'cause as a ghost writer, you
write in someone else's voice,

00:00:21.330 --> 00:00:24.160
so it was so exciting to tell my stories,

00:00:24.160 --> 00:00:26.590
and I wanted the book
to feel like a warm hug

00:00:26.590 --> 00:00:29.350
when you read it, and
so I hope people laugh,

00:00:29.350 --> 00:00:30.200
I hope they enjoy it.

00:00:30.200 --> 00:00:32.320
I think we all need our laughs
where we can get them now.

00:00:32.320 --> 00:00:35.180
So there's tons of pop
culture, there's nostalgia.

00:00:35.180 --> 00:00:37.720
There's a couple more
dramatic moments too.

00:00:37.720 --> 00:00:40.090
- What's your favorite pop
culture story in there?

00:00:40.090 --> 00:00:41.270
- The stories always change.

00:00:41.270 --> 00:00:42.870
My brain just thinks in pop culture.

00:00:42.870 --> 00:00:44.900
There was one birthday story
that I wrote about in the book.

00:00:44.900 --> 00:00:46.340
My boyfriend and I had
been together forever,

00:00:46.340 --> 00:00:48.130
and I'm not a big birthday person.

00:00:48.130 --> 00:00:50.150
We like to go to the
movies on my birthday.

00:00:50.150 --> 00:00:51.880
And a few years ago we went to the movies

00:00:51.880 --> 00:00:53.698
and Jonathan Groff.

00:00:53.698 --> 00:00:55.364
(Drew sighs)
- I mean, he's great, right?

00:00:55.364 --> 00:00:56.197
- I love him.

00:00:56.197 --> 00:00:59.070
- He was with Lea Michele,
both Broadway people.

00:00:59.070 --> 00:01:01.070
I think they were sitting in front of me,

00:01:01.070 --> 00:01:02.357
so in my head the whole
time we're watching,

00:01:02.357 --> 00:01:03.820
"A star is born" All I'm thinking is like,

00:01:03.820 --> 00:01:05.540
my boyfriend planned them to come sing

00:01:05.540 --> 00:01:07.170
happy birthday to me afterwards.

00:01:07.170 --> 00:01:08.760
So I'm sitting in, "A star is born"

00:01:08.760 --> 00:01:12.040
Practicing my excited
face for when they get up

00:01:12.040 --> 00:01:14.350
after the movie to sing happy birthday.

00:01:14.350 --> 00:01:18.550
Which was crazy, and that's
not what they were there for.

00:01:18.550 --> 00:01:21.860
And I got mad at my boyfriend
then when I finally realized

00:01:21.860 --> 00:01:23.260
that they weren't there to sing to me.

00:01:23.260 --> 00:01:24.880
I don't know what happened
in, "A star is born."

00:01:24.880 --> 00:01:26.390
I've obviously seen the original,

00:01:26.390 --> 00:01:27.900
I need to rewatch it, but
it was like, you know,

00:01:27.900 --> 00:01:31.380
you build things up, and
birthdays make us crazy, I think.

00:01:31.380 --> 00:01:35.080
We build things up in our
heads, we have such expectation.

00:01:35.080 --> 00:01:36.810
And so, you know, it's a little
more detailed in the book,

00:01:36.810 --> 00:01:39.900
but yeah, I thought these
Broadway people were there

00:01:39.900 --> 00:01:41.710
to sing heavy birthday, which is insane.

00:01:41.710 --> 00:01:44.933
And then I got mad at my
boyfriend for not doing that.

00:01:46.580 --> 00:01:47.770
They're not for hire.

00:01:47.770 --> 00:01:49.470
Jonathan Groff's not
like, he's not a clown.

00:01:49.470 --> 00:01:52.120
- You do mingle with fabulous people.

00:01:52.120 --> 00:01:54.920
I think anything might be
possible in your world, Danny.

00:01:55.830 --> 00:01:57.150
But did you forgive him?

00:01:57.150 --> 00:01:58.105
- No.

00:01:58.105 --> 00:01:59.340
(Drew and Ross laughing)

00:01:59.340 --> 00:02:00.190
- I love it.

00:02:00.190 --> 00:02:01.860
All right, well it's design week here,

00:02:01.860 --> 00:02:06.160
and when are Drew crew design
hero, Mikel Welch was here,

00:02:06.160 --> 00:02:09.810
he said the 90's are
coming back in home decor,

00:02:09.810 --> 00:02:12.620
and Danny, since you practically got a PhD

00:02:12.620 --> 00:02:15.320
in pop culture nostalgia,
we thought that we could dig

00:02:15.320 --> 00:02:18.690
into some stories where
design and nostalgia meet.

00:02:18.690 --> 00:02:19.798
Are you in?

00:02:19.798 --> 00:02:21.354
- I'm so excited.
- Okay, perfect.

00:02:21.354 --> 00:02:22.334
(crowd cheering)
(applause)

00:02:22.334 --> 00:02:23.440
All right, Danny, you're the first story.

00:02:23.440 --> 00:02:26.790
- Okay, so first up, some
people invest in Bitcoin,

00:02:26.790 --> 00:02:28.200
other people invest in Britney Spears.

00:02:28.200 --> 00:02:30.200
That's a currency I can get behind.

00:02:30.200 --> 00:02:32.530
The New York post reports a super fan

00:02:32.530 --> 00:02:35.640
named Zachary Gordon
Abraham has spent 20 years

00:02:35.640 --> 00:02:37.780
building a Britney bunker in his house.

00:02:37.780 --> 00:02:39.590
We're talking wall to
wall Brit collectibles.

00:02:39.590 --> 00:02:41.170
I love that, and it's now-

00:02:41.170 --> 00:02:42.290
- [Drew] Oh, it gets better, look at that.

00:02:42.290 --> 00:02:43.123
- [Danny] It's now-

00:02:43.123 --> 00:02:44.060
- [Drew] Can you believe that?

00:02:44.060 --> 00:02:47.740
- [Danny] I'd say undervalued at $137,000.

00:02:47.740 --> 00:02:49.258
- [Drew] I agree!

00:02:49.258 --> 00:02:51.100
- And that's not all,
Zachary even met his husband

00:02:51.100 --> 00:02:53.110
through their love of Britney Spears.

00:02:53.110 --> 00:02:54.690
Who doesn't love Britney Spears?

00:02:54.690 --> 00:02:57.220
- I love that he met his partner.

00:02:57.220 --> 00:02:58.925
(crowd cheering)
(applause)

00:02:58.925 --> 00:02:59.758
- I know.

00:02:59.758 --> 00:03:00.810
- And I get it too.

00:03:00.810 --> 00:03:02.220
I'm a pop culture collectible person,

00:03:02.220 --> 00:03:04.860
so I have my, the nanny
Barbie at my house.

00:03:04.860 --> 00:03:05.693
- Oh my God.

00:03:05.693 --> 00:03:06.526
- The Fran Drescher?

00:03:06.526 --> 00:03:07.800
- I love Fran Drescher.

00:03:07.800 --> 00:03:09.470
I have a Rosie O'Donnell Barbie.

00:03:09.470 --> 00:03:10.303
Remember she had?

00:03:10.303 --> 00:03:12.050
We need to get, do you have a Barbie?

00:03:12.050 --> 00:03:13.100
Charlie's angels Barbie.

00:03:13.100 --> 00:03:15.000
- We have Charlie's angels dolls, yeah.

00:03:15.000 --> 00:03:18.080
- Well this guy wanted to stop
collecting Britney's stuff

00:03:18.080 --> 00:03:20.637
but he bought one more,
and you know what he said?

00:03:20.637 --> 00:03:22.125
"Oops, I did it again."

00:03:22.125 --> 00:03:24.600
- Aha!
(crowd applauds)

00:03:24.600 --> 00:03:28.120
All right, next we're gonna
go to the shaggadelic 70's.

00:03:28.120 --> 00:03:31.230
Insider reports a woman
named Charlie Leanna Murphy

00:03:31.230 --> 00:03:35.600
was so inspired by Jayne
Mansfield's pink shag look

00:03:35.600 --> 00:03:38.030
that she created her own pink penthouse.

00:03:38.030 --> 00:03:39.370
Look at this.

00:03:39.370 --> 00:03:41.910
Look, it features pink glittered doors

00:03:41.910 --> 00:03:43.880
and shag, shag, shag everywhere,

00:03:43.880 --> 00:03:45.610
and it's not just wall to wall,

00:03:45.610 --> 00:03:47.710
it's floor to ceiling too.

00:03:47.710 --> 00:03:48.690
- [Drew] Wow.

00:03:48.690 --> 00:03:50.380
- [Danny] I feel like I need
a Claritin just looking-

00:03:50.380 --> 00:03:51.570
- [Ross] Exactly.

00:03:51.570 --> 00:03:52.910
- [Drew] Ironically.

00:03:52.910 --> 00:03:54.950
- [Ross] Yeah, well she
says she has to vacuum

00:03:54.950 --> 00:03:58.400
every single day to make sure
the air doesn't get too shaggy

00:03:58.400 --> 00:03:59.720
and dusty.

00:03:59.720 --> 00:04:01.680
Yeah, that's a lot of shag carpet.

00:04:01.680 --> 00:04:04.540
- It's funny, my friend, Jamie
Nelson, she's a photographer,

00:04:04.540 --> 00:04:06.900
she shoots all of our
flower beauty campaign.

00:04:06.900 --> 00:04:07.950
She's amazing.

00:04:07.950 --> 00:04:09.710
This is her bathroom.

00:04:09.710 --> 00:04:10.670
That is not a joke.

00:04:10.670 --> 00:04:14.061
She is the coolest chick on the planet.

00:04:14.061 --> 00:04:15.981
(crowd cheers)
(applause)

00:04:15.981 --> 00:04:18.250
I thought it was her house
that we were talking about

00:04:18.250 --> 00:04:19.140
for a minute.

00:04:19.140 --> 00:04:21.950
I love when people go for it.

00:04:21.950 --> 00:04:22.960
- [Danny] Yeah, totally.

00:04:22.960 --> 00:04:25.590
- I love that all in factor.

00:04:25.590 --> 00:04:30.240
In fact, staying and moving
to the 1970s for a minute,

00:04:30.240 --> 00:04:33.430
the Daily Mail reports, a
young guy in the UK longed

00:04:33.430 --> 00:04:37.250
for that perfect cozy 70's feel
of his grandparents' house,

00:04:37.250 --> 00:04:39.240
so he totally transformed his living space

00:04:39.240 --> 00:04:41.440
into a 1970's cocoon.

00:04:41.440 --> 00:04:44.150
- [Ross] So cool.
- He spent, listen $3,000.

00:04:44.150 --> 00:04:46.220
I know that sounds like a lot of money,

00:04:46.220 --> 00:04:48.430
but he was able to redo his entire house.

00:04:48.430 --> 00:04:52.200
He bought everything secondhand
on eBay and Facebook,

00:04:52.200 --> 00:04:55.350
and then created this total time warp.

00:04:55.350 --> 00:04:57.710
I think he did a fantastic job for-

00:04:57.710 --> 00:04:59.840
- [Ross] I love it.
(applause)

00:04:59.840 --> 00:05:04.150
- I have this fantasy of doing
like a late 90's inspired,

00:05:04.150 --> 00:05:05.820
so I wanna get the inflatable furniture,

00:05:05.820 --> 00:05:08.620
and I always had a dream of,
having one of those MacBooks

00:05:08.620 --> 00:05:11.210
we never got, do you know
the colorful MacBook?

00:05:11.210 --> 00:05:12.043
- Yeah.

00:05:12.043 --> 00:05:13.264
- I wanted one of those so bad.

00:05:13.264 --> 00:05:15.030
- And like, the full box one?

00:05:15.030 --> 00:05:17.370
- My dream, Drew, was to sit
in front of that computer,

00:05:17.370 --> 00:05:19.000
watch Charlie's angels on the TV,

00:05:19.000 --> 00:05:21.210
and sit on my inflatable furniture.

00:05:21.210 --> 00:05:23.760
That's all I want, is a late 90's.

00:05:23.760 --> 00:05:27.184
- Danny, I think we
could make this happen.

00:05:27.184 --> 00:05:29.851
(upbeat music)

